-- title:
--   A locally constant GtimesFin 2 label on rigidified points
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ and $\bar r$ are primes with $\bar r\neq r$ (`hrr`), and $N$ is a non-zero squarefree integer divisible by neither (`hrN`, `hrbarN`, `hN`).
--
--   **Local base data.** $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain that is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with irreducible element $\pi$ (`hπ`), is $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), has residue ring of cardinality $r$ (`hres`) and satisfies $(r)=(\pi)$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Next, $Onr$ is a characteristic-zero domain and $\mathcal O$-algebra with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, such that $Onr$ is $\pi$-adically complete (`hOnr_complete`), $(\pi)$ is maximal in $Onr$ (`hOnr_max`), every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $Onr$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $Fr(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod\pi$ (`hFr`): thus $Onr$ is a complete unramified extension with algebraically closed residue field and $Fr$ lifts the $r$-power Frobenius. The homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet}\colon GL_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ is pinned down by `hvdet`: $\mathrm{vdet}(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^{\times}$.
--
--   **Shimura-curve side.** $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is indefinite and ramified exactly at $r,\bar r$ (`hB`), $\Lambda$ is a maximal order (`hΛ`), and every rational integer lies in $\Lambda$ (`hΛℤ`). The scheme $\mathcal X$ with $f\colon\mathcal X\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and the point assignment `pt` is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with $\Gamma_0(N)$-data in the sense of `IsCoarseModuli` (isomorphism invariance, pullback compatibility, bijectivity on algebraically closed points, universal property) (`h𝒳`). The auxiliary level satisfies $n\ge 3$, $r\nmid n$, $\bar r\nmid n$, $\gcd(n,N)=1$; $M$ with $fM$ and `ptF` is a fine moduli space for curves with full level-$n$ structure (`hM`), and $\rho\colon G\to\operatorname{Aut}M$, $\chi\colon G\to\Lambda$ form a level-twist action (`hρ`: the automorphisms are $\mathcal O$-linear, they realise twisting of the level structure by $\chi$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, injective and surjective modulo $n$). The morphism $p\colon M\to\mathcal X$ lies over $\mathcal O$ (`hp`), is $G$-invariant (`hρp`) and forgets the level-$n$ structure on points (`hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell\neq r,\bar r$, $\mathcal Y_\ell$ with $g_\ell$ and `ptT` is a coarse moduli space for curves with extra level-$\ell$ structure (`h𝒴`), and $d_0,d_1\colon\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ lie over $\mathcal O$ (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) and induce, on points, the forgetful map (`hd₀`) and the quotient by a level-$\ell$ isogeny (`hd₁`). The morphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}\colon\mathcal X\to\mathcal X$ lie over $\mathcal O$ (`harf`, `harbarf`) and induce the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite quaternion side.** $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$ (`hdef`), with $\Lambda_1$ maximal, $R_1\subseteq\Lambda_1$ Eichler of level $N$ (`hΛ₁`, `hR₁`, `hRΛ₁`), $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ (`hn₁`) with $\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1)$ Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`), and $\iota_0$ an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding into $M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`); $v$ is the place above $r$ (`hv`). The group $\Gamma^t$ is the group of units integral away from $v$ (`hΓt`); the elements $s_\ell$ and finite ideles $s^{f}_\ell$ satisfy `hs` (four clauses: $s^{f}_\ell$ agrees with $s_\ell$ away from $r$, is $1$ at $r$, the product of the diagonal $\ell$ with $(s^{f}_\ell)^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet` or `primeHeckeSet` at $\ell$ according as $\ell\mid N$ or not, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$), with $\Gamma^t_\ell=\Gamma^t\cap s_\ell\Gamma^t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`); $\bar w$ has reduced norm $\bar r$ and normalises $\Gamma^t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **Special fibre and its uniformisation data.** `coord`$\colon\Lambda\to W(\mathbb F_{r^2})^2$ is an order coordinate (`hcoord`: additive, $1\mapsto(1,0)$, the twisted product rule, injective, dense modulo every power of $r$, and compatible with traces). Over the residue ring $Onr/\pi$ there are a fake elliptic curve $A_0$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of $A_0$ in two variables with $A_0$ a formal module via `coord`, $X_0$, $\theta_0$ (`hA₀`), and families $e,e'$ of endomorphisms of $A_0$ indexed by $\Gamma^t$ over the base (`he`) with degrees `deg`. The hypotheses `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4` (summarised here) state: each pair $(e_\gamma,e'_\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure; $e$ is multiplicative and sends rational scalars to scalars, up to multiplication by powers of $r$, and only scalars of $\Gamma^t$ act as integers; for every injective matrix realisation $E_0$ of the centraliser of the $W(\mathbb F_{r^2})$-action and of $\varpi$ on $X_0$ there is $g\in GL_2(K_0)$ such that each $e_\gamma$ is induced on $\theta_0$ by an element of that centraliser whose image is $r^{k_\gamma}g\,\iota_0(\gamma)g^{-1}$; the action of $e$ on a full level-$n$ structure of $A_0$ is given by a $\Lambda$-valued cocycle modulo $n$; and every $r$-power isogeny preserving the level of a fake elliptic curve over an algebraically closed field pulled back from $A_0$ comes from some $e_\gamma$ up to $r$-powers. Further, $R_2\subseteq R_1$ is an order (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`) with $r$-power denominators over $R_1$ (`hR₂r`) and $\hat e$ extends the construction to $R_2$ over the base (`hê`), the clauses `hE5a`–`hE5e` (summarised here) asserting that $\hat e$ is additive, $\Lambda$-equivariant and level-preserving, is a monoid map sending $1$ to the identity, integers to the corresponding scalars, and a pair $(x,\bar x)$ to multiplication by $\mathrm{nrd}(x)$, agrees with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma^t$, and is realised on $\theta_0$ by the same conjugated matrix normalisation as $e$.
--
--   **Drinfeld side.** $\iota\colon W(\mathbb F_{r^2})\to Onr$, $\Phi$ is a special (`hΦ`) formal $\mathcal O_D$-module of height $4$ (`hΦ4`) over $Onr/r$, `MD` is a moduli package which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`), and $\eta$ compares rigidified objects with `MD`, the three clauses of `hη` asserting that $\eta$ separates admissible rigidified objects exactly up to isomorphism, is natural in the base, and is locally surjective. The homomorphism $E_0$ is injective and almost surjective onto a scaled copy of $M_2(\mathcal O)$ (`hE₀`). The family $eD$ together with `hnatD`, `hbijD`, `hfstD`, `hGLD`, `hPiD`, `hPiexD` identifies, naturally and bijectively, the functor of `GPoint`s of `MD` with the product of the functor corepresented by $Onr$ and Deligne's lattice-line functor $\Omega$, compatibly with the first projection, with the twisted $GL_2(K_0)$-action and with $\pi$-translation, $\pi$-translates being always available. Finally $\kappa$ is the comparison of residue rings (`hκ`) and $\beta_0$ is an isogeny $\Phi\to X_0$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`); $P_0$ is a full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner datum on the special fibre.** $A_{0w}$ with $aw,aw'$ realises the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), $(bw,bw')$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ preserving the level (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), the compatibilities `haw`, `haw'`, `hbw`, `habw` hold over the base, and `hJOINTw` states that for every injective matrix realisation of the centraliser there is a single $g\in GL_2(K_0)$ conjugating the action of each $\gamma\in\Gamma^t$ to $e_\gamma$ and the action of $\bar w$ to $aw$ followed by $bw$, in both cases up to a power of $r$.
--
--   **The map to the Drinfeld functor.** $\Xi$ assigns to a rigidified curve over a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and a structure map $\psi\colon Onr\to B$ a `GPoint` of `MD`, subject to `hΞleg` (over connected $B$ the leg of $\Xi$ is $\psi\circ Fr^{k}$ for some $k\in\mathbb Z$), `hΞnat` (compatibility with pullbacks of rigidified curves), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of rigidified curves matched by an $r$-power correspondence of the rigidifications), and `hΞdef` (over connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent, if the curve carries a formal module structure $(X,\theta)$ via `coord`, then $\Xi$ is computed as $\eta$ applied to an admissible rigidified object $t$ with $t.X=X$ which is a rig-transport of $\theta_0$ along $\kappa,\beta_0$ with exponent $j\le1$, the leg being $\psi\circ Fr^{-j}$). The element $g_0\in GL_2(K_0)$ satisfies `heqΓ` (translating a rigidification by $e_\gamma$ corresponds, up to a power of $r$, to the action of $g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ on $\Xi$) and `heqW` (when $\bar r$ is invertible, an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ matched by the $r$-power correspondence built from $aw\,bw$ corresponds to the action of $g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$).
--
--   **The abstract point functor.** $C$ is a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra in which $\pi$ is nilpotent (`hCπ`), $\chi_C\colon Onr\to C$ is an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, $PR$ is a functor on commutative $C$-algebras, and `ptR` assigns a point of $PR(S)$ to each $C$-algebra $S$ with compatible $\mathcal O$-structure, each $\psi_S$ equal to $\chi_C$ followed by $C\to S$, each curve with full level-$n$ structure $u$ over $S$ and each rigidification $\rho$ of $u.1$ relative to $A_0$ and $\psi_S$. The hypotheses are: `hR2` (`ptR` is compatible with pullback along $C$-algebra maps of curves, level structures and rigidifications), `hR3s` (`ptR` is surjective onto $PR(S)$), `hR3i` (over $S$ with only trivial idempotents, two presentations of the same point are linked by an isomorphism of curves-with-level and a comparison of the rigidifications up to an $r$-power correspondence), and `hR1` (the converse: such an isomorphism and comparison force equality of the `ptR`-values).
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a labelling `lab` assigning to every commutative Noetherian $C$-algebra $S$, every witness that the only idempotents of $S$ are $0$ and $1$, and every $x\in PR(S)$, an element of $G\times\mathbf{Fin}\,2$, such that the following five statements hold.
--
--   (i) *Naturality.* For Noetherian $C$-algebras $S$ and $S'$ with only trivial idempotents, $S'$ non-trivial, every $C$-algebra map $g\colon S\to S'$ and every $x\in PR(S)$, one has $\mathrm{lab}_{S'}(PR(g)x)=\mathrm{lab}_S(x)$.
--
--   (ii) *Presentations determine the label.* Let $S$ be a non-trivial Noetherian $C$-algebra with only trivial idempotents, carrying a compatible $\mathcal O$-algebra structure, let $x\in PR(S)$, $g\in G$ and $j\in\mathbf{Fin}\,2$. Suppose $\pi$ is nilpotent in $S$ and there are $\psi_S\colon Onr\to S$ equal to $\chi_C$ followed by $C\to S$, a curve with full level-$n$ structure $u$ over $S$ and a rigidification $\rho$ of $u.1$ with $\mathrm{ptR}(u,\rho)=x$, such that some full level-$n$ structure $P_n$ on $u.1$ is a norm level transport of $P_0$ along $\rho$ (in the sense of `IsNormLevelTransport` for the data $Fr,\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0,\Phi,\iota,\mathrm{coord}$) with the level structure of $u$ equal to $P_n$ followed by the action of $\chi(g)$, and such that the leg of $\Xi_S(\psi_S)(u.1,\rho)$ is $\psi_S\circ Fr^{-j}$. Then $\mathrm{lab}_S(x)=(g,j)$.
--
--   (iii) *Over local rings the label is attained.* If in addition $S$ is a local Noetherian $C$-algebra with compatible $\mathcal O$-structure and only trivial idempotents, and $\mathrm{lab}_S(x)=(g,j)$, then data as in (ii) exist: $\pi$ nilpotent in $S$, a structure map $\psi_S$, a curve with level $u$, a rigidification $\rho$ with $\mathrm{ptR}(u,\rho)=x$, a norm level transport $P_n$ of $P_0$ along $\rho$ with the level structure of $u$ equal to $P_n$ followed by the action of $\chi(g)$, and the leg of $\Xi_S(\psi_S)(u.1,\rho)$ equal to $\psi_S\circ Fr^{-j}$.
--
--   (iv) *Parity read-off on every presentation.* For every non-trivial Noetherian $C$-algebra $S$ with compatible $\mathcal O$-structure and only trivial idempotents, with $\pi$ nilpotent in $S$, every structure map $\psi_S$, every curve with full level-$n$ structure $u$ and every rigidification $\rho$ of $u.1$, the leg of $\Xi_S(\psi_S)(u.1,\rho)$ equals $\psi_S\circ Fr^{-j}$ where $j$ is the second component of $\mathrm{lab}_S(\mathrm{ptR}(u,\rho))$.
--
--   (v) *Transitivity in the group component.* For every non-trivial Noetherian $C$-algebra $S$ with compatible $\mathcal O$-structure and only trivial idempotents, every structure map $\psi_S$, every curve with full level-$n$ structure $u$, every rigidification $\rho$ of $u.1$ and every $g_1\in G$, there is a full level-$n$ structure $P'$ on the same curve $u.1$ with $\mathrm{lab}_S(\mathrm{ptR}((u.1,P'),\rho))=(g_1,j)$, where $j$ is the second component of $\mathrm{lab}_S(\mathrm{ptR}(u,\rho))$.
--
--   This is the labelling step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the Shimura curve attached to an indefinite quaternion algebra ramified at $r$ and $\bar r$: points of the rigidified moduli functor over a connected base are tagged by a pair consisting of the level-twisting element of $G$ and the Frobenius parity of the leg of the associated Drinfeld point, the tag being locally constant and exact on presentations. It is used by the two results establishing existence and uniqueness of the even rigidified pair when $2$ is invertible.
